+# vimbubble/v2
+
+[![ci](https://github.com/guygrigsby/vimbubble/actions/workflows/ci.yml/badge.svg)](https://github.com/guygrigsby/vimbubble/actions/workflows/ci.yml)
+[![Go Reference](https://pkg.go.dev/badge/github.com/guygrigsby/vimbubble/v2.svg)](https://pkg.go.dev/github.com/guygrigsby/vimbubble/v2)
+
+Vim-style modal editing for [bubbles v2](https://github.com/charmbracelet/bubbles) textareas.
+
+Drop it next to an existing `textarea.Model`, route key presses through it, get NORMAL/INSERT/VISUAL modes and the verbs you'd expect — `i`, `a`, `o`, `x`, `~`, `r`, `dw`, `cw`, `c$`, `cc`, `v`, `V`, `y`, `p`, and friends.
+
+```
+go get github.com/guygrigsby/vimbubble/v2
+```
+
+Targets `charm.land/bubbles/v2` and `charm.land/bubbletea/v2`. For the v1 line (`github.com/charmbracelet/bubbles`), see the module at the repository root.
+
+## What changed from v1
+
+- Public cursor API. v1 read the textarea's unexported `row`/`col` through `reflect`+`unsafe`; v2 uses `Line()`, `Column()`, `SetCursorColumn()`, `CursorUp()`, `CursorDown()`, `CursorStart()`, `CursorEnd()`. A test (`TestNoReflectNoUnsafe`) keeps it that way.
+- VISUAL mode (`v`, `V`) backed by the textarea's own selection, so it renders with the textarea's selection style and the host can read it through `Selection()` / `SelectedText()`.
+- A yank register: `y` in VISUAL fills it, `d`/`x`/`c` fill it with what they cut, `p` in NORMAL pastes it.
+- `Update` takes `tea.KeyPressMsg` and returns a single `tea.Cmd` rather than a slice.
+- `Position()` / `SetPosition()` expose the cursor to the host.
+
+## Quick start
+
+```go
+import (
+    "charm.land/bubbles/v2/textarea"
+    tea "charm.land/bubbletea/v2"
+    vimbubble "github.com/guygrigsby/vimbubble/v2"
+)
+
+type model struct {
+    ta  textarea.Model
+    vim *vimbubble.Modal
+}
+
+func initial() model {
+    ta := textarea.New()
+    m := model{ta: ta}
+    m.vim = vimbubble.New(&m.ta)
+    m.vim.SetEnabled(true)   // off by default; opt in
+    return m
+}
+
+func (m model) Update(msg tea.Msg) (tea.Model, tea.Cmd) {
+    if k, ok := msg.(tea.KeyPressMsg); ok {
+        // Modal eats the key when it has a binding; otherwise the
+        // textarea handles it as usual.
+        if consumed, cmd := m.vim.Update(k); consumed {
+            return m, cmd
+        }
+    }
+    var cmd tea.Cmd
+    m.ta, cmd = m.ta.Update(msg)
+    return m, cmd
+}
+
+func (m model) View() string {
+    return m.vim.ModeLabel() + "\n" + m.ta.View()
+}
+```
+
+`vim.SetEnabled(false)` disables vim mode entirely — every key passes through to the textarea unmodified, perfect for a `/vim` toggle in your app.
+
+## Supported commands
+
+### NORMAL mode
+
+| Key       | What it does                                 |
+|-----------|----------------------------------------------|
+| `h` `l`   | cursor left / right                          |
+| `j` `k`   | cursor down / up                             |
+| `w` `b`   | word forward / backward                      |
+| `0` `$`   | line start / end                             |
+| `gg` `G`  | buffer top / bottom                          |
+| `x`       | delete character forward                     |
+| `D`       | delete to end of line                        |
+| `~`       | toggle case of char + advance                |
+| `r<x>`    | replace char under cursor with `<x>`         |
+| `p`       | paste the register after the cursor          |
+| `dd`      | delete whole line                            |
+| `dw`      | delete word forward                          |
+| `d$` `d0` | delete to end / start of line                |
+| `cw`      | change word (delete + INSERT)                |
+| `c$` `c0` | change to end / start of line                |
+| `cc`      | empty the line + INSERT                      |
+| `ciw`     | change inside word (any cursor position) + INSERT |
+| `caw`     | change a word + its surrounding space + INSERT |
+| `diw`     | delete inside word                           |
+| `daw`     | delete a word + its surrounding space        |
+| `i` `a`   | INSERT at / after cursor                     |
+| `I` `A`   | INSERT at line start / end                   |
+| `o` `O`   | open new line below / above + INSERT         |
+| `v` `V`   | VISUAL from the cursor / over the whole line |
+| `/` `:`   | INSERT mode + insert the literal character (lets host apps reach a slash-command palette without first pressing `i`) |
+
+### VISUAL mode
+
+| Key                     | What it does                            |
+|-------------------------|-----------------------------------------|
+| `h` `l` `j` `k` `w` `b` `0` `$` `G` | extend the selection        |
+| `d` `x`                 | delete the selection, back to NORMAL    |
+| `y`                     | yank the selection, back to NORMAL      |
+| `c`                     | delete the selection, into INSERT       |
+| `V`                     | linewise VISUAL over the current row     |
+| `v`                     | charwise from the cursor (narrows a linewise selection; leaves VISUAL when already charwise) |
+| `Esc`                   | drop the selection, back to NORMAL      |
+
+VISUAL is inclusive of the character under the cursor, so `v` straight into an operator acts on that character, at the end of a line included.
+
+`V` makes VISUAL linewise: the cursor stays on its own row, motions grow the selection by whole rows between the anchor row and the cursor's, and the range takes the newline that ends it, so `Vjd` removes both rows instead of blanking them (on the buffer's last row it takes the preceding newline, as vim does). An operator with nothing to act on leaves the mode alone rather than reporting a change that didn't happen.
+
+### INSERT mode
+
+Every key passes through to the textarea, except **Esc** which returns to NORMAL.
+
+## What's not (yet) here
+
+- Named registers (`"a`, `"+`) and linewise paste
+- Undo / redo
+- Search (`/<query>` as a search, not a passthrough)
+- Find-character motions (`f`, `t`, `F`, `T`)
+- Non-word text objects (`it`, `i"`, `i(`)
+- Counts (`3dd`)
+- `gg` inside VISUAL
+- Jump list (`Ctrl+O`, `Ctrl+I`)
+
+These are reasonable next chunks. Open an issue if you want one, or send a PR.
+
+## How it works
+
+Motions move the textarea's cursor through its public API; the verbs the textarea already implements (`x`, `D`, `dd`, `d0`, `o`) are synthesised as `tea.KeyPressMsg` and forwarded to `textarea.Update`; the rest (`~`, `r`, `cw`, `ciw`, …) edit `Value()`/`SetValue()` and re-pin the cursor.
+
+VISUAL mode drives the textarea's selection. `BeginSelection` and `ExtendSelection` take *rendered* coordinates (screen cells from the textarea's top-left, gutter included, soft-wrapped rows counted from the top of the viewport), not buffer positions, and everything that maps between the two is unexported. `selectionPoint` therefore inverts `PositionAt` with a binary search on each axis — the mapping is monotone, so it lands exactly, wrapped lines and scrolled viewports included.
+
+## License
+
+MIT
